course: dictionary
lesson: 7169
title: A word from the frozen north
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: You can work out a new word by reading the words around it, which are its context. «Permafrost is ground that stays frozen all year» tells you what permafrost is: ground, which is soil, that stays frozen all the time.
explain: Now look at the place. «Lyuba, a baby mammoth, was found in Siberian permafrost» shows that permafrost is found in very cold places, such as Siberia. A frozen place in the far north is a good clue to what the word means.
explain: Clues can also come after the word. «In summer only a thin top layer thaws into mud» tells you that thaws means melts, and that the ground underneath stays frozen. To check your meaning, swap it in: frozen ground that stays frozen all year still makes sense.
fact: Permafrost is ground that stays frozen all year round for at least two years in a row.
fact: Permafrost is found in very cold places such as the Arctic, Siberia, Alaska and northern Canada.
fact: «Thaws» means melts, so in summer only the thin top layer of permafrost melts into mud.
fact: Scientists have found frozen woolly mammoths and ancient seeds in permafrost.
fact: When permafrost melts, buildings can sink and roads can crack, which is one way global warming shows up.
exercise: «Frozen ground called permafrost works like a freezer.» What is permafrost? | A thick forest of tall trees | Warm sand on a beach | A lake that dries up in summer | *Ground that stays frozen all year round
exercise: «In summer only a thin top layer thaws into mud.» What does thaws mean? | Grows tall | Freezes solid | Splits in two | *Melts
exercise: Where was Lyuba the baby mammoth found? | In the Sahara Desert | On the beach in Sydney | *In Siberian permafrost | In the middle of the Amazon rainforest
test: Why was Lyuba, the baby mammoth, found almost whole? | Because she was made of stone | Because she swam to the surface | *Because the frozen permafrost kept her safe | Because she was buried in hot sand
test: What happens to buildings when permafrost melts? | They grow taller | *They sink | They float away | They become stronger
exam: Using the clues in the lesson, what is permafrost? | A kind of cold, wet sea | *Ground that stays frozen for at least two years in a row | Ground that thaws every summer | A type of mammoth
